       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects would last for days.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the standard maximum.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated up to 10 mg.\n- **30 mg total daily from several agents**, if you meant a combination regimen or a different drug.\n- **30 mg is correct**, for example because of an unusual clinical situation. If so, please confirm it, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional.\n\nI'll enter the order as soon as you tell me which one."
      }
